15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Flowchart detailing the selection of final PTMC patient cohort: 1,356 PTMC patients were considered, with exclusions for multifocality, other malignant tumors, ultrasound-pathology discrepancy, incomplete clinical data, and poor ultrasound image quality, resulting in 432 patients divided into training \(259 patients, 60 percent\) and validation sets \(173 patients, 40 percent\).) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Ultrasound image labeled panel A shows a longitudinal section of the thyroid gland divided by dashed lines into superior, middle, and inferior poles. Panel B presents another thyroid ultrasound view with a measurement marker indicating a papillary thyroid microcarcinoma nodule.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays a receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curve for age with a cut-off at thirty-eight years, while panel B shows ROC curves for maximum lesion diameter and volume with cut-offs at zero point nine seven five centimeters and zero point one six one cubic centimeters, respectively. Each panel includes a diagonal reference line.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Nomogram graphic for predicting CLNM rate using variables: age, HT, tumor location, maximum diameter over 0.95 cm, microcalcification, suspicious lateral lymph node \(LLN\), and suspicious central lymph node \(CLN\), with corresponding points, total points, linear predictor, and CLNM rate scales.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a training set ROC curve with an AUC of 0.772, and panel B shows a validation set ROC curve with an AUC of 0.728; both indicate model discrimination. Panel C displays a calibration curve for the training set comparing apparent, bias-corrected, and ideal probabilities, while panel D presents a similar calibration curve for the validation set. Panel E illustrates a decision curve analysis for net benefit versus high risk threshold, comparing the model, all, and none strategies. Panel F is a forest plot comparing intergroup risk differences using Tukey\220s test, displaying log odds ratios and confidence intervals for three group comparisons.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
